  This is basically Neovim configured from scratch without needing any external
plugin. Everything utilities is written directly in Lua. However, there are some
dependencies optionally to enable file searching which is ripgrep, and the
required Neovim version is at least 0.11. This configurations features are can
be seen in lua/module directory, each file represent a utility, and is loaded
at startup (see init.lua). The lua/core directory is just my opinionated options
which can be changed however you like it. The lsp folder is for configuring lsp
which is posibble since version 0.11, and there are already two lsp configured.
and lastly the colors folder is just the default color theme that I make my own
specially for this config.

  To use this config, just clone this repository into your desired config
directory by the name nvim, in Linux system this is usually ~/.config/nvim, in
Windows this is usually %LOCALAPPDATA%/nvim, I don't know much about MacOS.
After that, you can just rerun you Neovim and it should be just fine, there's no
installing anything after it, what you see here is all it needs except for the
optional ripgrep I mentioned.
